   218	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   219	    """
   220	    Swap every sprite to the opposite prototype, snap it to the nearest extrapolated guide anchor, and expand the canvas only when needed.
   221	
   222	    Input structure:
   223	    - bg = most common color. A separate guide color forms a visible 3x3 lattice of singleton dots with uniform row/col spacing.
   224	    - Two distinct small sprite patterns appear at integer scales, and each sprite contains color-1 anchor cells.
   225	    - Sprites are placed inside Voronoi cells of that lattice, so some are nearest to an anchor that lies just outside the visible 3x3 block.
   226	
